values ('a7b8c9d0-1e2f-4a74-9b34-4d5e6f7a8b44', 'child-development', 'Child Development', 'Frame child development as an evidence-based study of change in children within relationships, cultures, schools, and communities. Topics cover research methods and ethics, major theories, prenatal development and early brain architecture, infancy, attachment, and temperament, physical and health development, cognition and executive function, language and literacy, social-emotional development, family, peers, and developmental relationships, culture and ecological systems, play and motivation, middle childhood and schooling, neurodiversity, risk, resilience, and trauma, and developmentally appropriate practice.');

