  'Frame child development as an evidence-based study of change in children within relationships, cultures, schools, and communities. Topics cover research methods and ethics, major theories, prenatal development and early brain architecture, infancy, attachment, and temperament, physical and health development, cognition and executive function, language and literacy, social-emotional development, family, peers, and developmental relationships, culture and ecological systems, play and motivation, middle childhood and schooling, neurodiversity, risk, resilience, and trauma, and developmentally appropriate practice.',
  $chdvjson${"slug": "child-development", "title": "Child Development", "description": "Frame child development as an evidence-based study of change in children within relationships, cultures, schools, and communities. Topics cover research methods and ethics, major theories, prenatal development and early brain architecture, infancy, attachment, and temperament, physical and health development, cognition and executive function, language and literacy, social-emotional development, family, peers, and developmental relationships, culture and ecological systems, play and motivation, middle childhood and schooling, neurodiversity, risk, resilience, and trauma, and developmentally appropriate practice.", "topics": [{"id": "24764b4e-e840-482a-90d0-b71896b1cd84", "type": "topic", "title": "Child Development as a Field: Questions, Methods, and Ethics", "description": "Frame child development as an evidence-based study of change in children within relationships, cultures, schools, and communities.", "children": [{"id": "73d1cd02-5c3f-468a-9c2f-c2534503c48e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core Questions", "children": [{"id": "9a5299ee-650f-4eda-b149-50e69c7c3df0", "type": "concept", "title": "Nature and nurture"}, {"id": "940b0f24-3033-41fb-9476-f223cec1dee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity and discontinuity"}, {"id": "aef27e58-5aea-41aa-96bb-3fe3fd3aa2ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual differences"}, {"id": "8e486a5f-0b1e-407c-95cd-4e4617167aa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Developmental pathways"}], "description": "Students begin by asking what changes in childhood, why it changes, and how context shapes developmental pathways."}, {"id": "d0a7b883-d67d-42eb-9477-b7789818c9de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research Methods with Children", "children": [{"id": "448d138b-2893-4297-8518-3a613ff05bfd", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation"}, {"id": "a707278c-26a7-49bc-abd2-e634ce8c30f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Experiments and quasi-experiments"}, {"id": "5598a43f-1df8-4409-a28b-2bd4c9a3b633", "type": "concept", "title": "Longitudinal and cross-sectional designs"}, {"id": "e9a45b34-b3af-4521-b089-8d48bc2cb063", "type": "concept", "title": "Child assent and caregiver consent"}], "description": "Child development requires methods that fit children's abilities while protecting their rights and dignity."}, {"id": "6b64b24b-e35b-4430-bde4-4f419fd2aa64", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical and Practical Interpretation", "children": [{"id": "e6125a26-6573-4101-b833-11f0ed28d32c", "type": "concept", "title": "Deficit vs strengths framing"}, {"id": "34daa164-21de-44d6-809c-eab3c50adf92", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy"}, {"id": "c4f574d0-d35e-443f-bb24-6ee08467c691", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias in measurement"}, {"id": "a9d23495-b975-48c1-a395-c84167b7667d", "type": "concept", "title": "Application limits"}], "description": "Developmental findings must be interpreted without labeling children narrowly or ignoring culture and opportunity."}]}, {"id": "8971cc1a-10c8-4ddb-8391-0e615c796ff4", "type": "topic", "title": "Major Theories of Development and Learning", "description": "Compare classic and contemporary theories that explain how children grow, learn, relate, and adapt.", "children": [{"id": "61327478-8986-4a17-a4d4-e1f25c14736d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cognitive and Constructivist Theories", "children": [{"id": "9d0bb446-a0d1-4915-9155-f891c4ee5015", "type": "concept", "title": "Piaget"}, {"id": "22ef0ede-091b-422c-97c7-f9acc94097e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Schemas"}, {"id": "777192b2-c664-40a2-984c-9cf80a6a3301", "type": "concept", "title": "Stages"}, {"id": "d0021de4-a780-4586-87f6-7c0ac58c3173", "type": "concept", "title": "Constructivism"}], "description": "Cognitive theories explain how children actively build knowledge through experience and changing mental structures."}, {"id": "ea87dd45-a5a9-4613-af17-4dcad865ef3f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sociocultural and Psychosocial Theories", "children": [{"id": "ef0d4bb1-19e7-4654-948c-3dc850304281", "type": "concept", "title": "Vygotsky"}, {"id": "2d70ef8c-b546-4402-8d15-3c79ade6197e", "type": "concept", "title": "Zone of proximal development"}, {"id": "461c69b3-43b6-40b1-acd4-b215b4debe7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Erikson"}, {"id": "e00cdcd5-f933-462e-8806-4142abb042fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Scaffolding"}], "description": "These theories emphasize relationships, culture, language, identity, and social participation."}, {"id": "a10091d1-2a74-4442-933e-ccfdc652894d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Learning, Ecological, and Systems Theories", "children": [{"id": "6dc5fc2f-f0d8-4f26-9577-cd4886d7faae", "type": "concept", "title": "Behaviorism and social learning"}, {"id": "7fe31fd0-dfaa-4e99-ac44-d0a61caea443", "type": "concept", "title": "Bronfenbrenner"}, {"id": "f6597b3a-8f41-4aa7-9e67-a57c4a103c0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Developmental systems"}, {"id": "57d4d3d0-98e6-452a-acd5-cc78df058174", "type": "concept", "title": "Transactional models"}], "description": "Modern developmental thinking connects learning processes to families, schools, communities, biology, and time."}]}, {"id": "4d86a9bb-e244-48be-b2d4-c93c40665bdb", "type": "topic", "title": "Prenatal Development, Birth, and Early Brain Architecture", "description": "Understand how early biological foundations, environments, and caregiving shape developmental trajectories.", "children": [{"id": "4cba785c-2e6f-4b51-88a9-6a641f3f608f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prenatal Development", "children": [{"id": "0f859a70-fa78-4dd8-8f50-6a1cd5e8553e", "type": "concept", "title": "Germinal, embryonic, fetal periods"}, {"id": "1bf19c0b-d0d3-4bac-800c-8b93d40a2025", "type": "concept", "title": "Teratogens"}, {"id": "e61b915a-e85a-4a62-a33c-8dd69bbe0727", "type": "concept", "title": "Maternal health"}, {"id": "bc5dda87-0997-40e5-8c95-a1651d2e66cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Prenatal stress"}], "description": "Prenatal development