: "Joint attention"}, {"id": "66482e91-f0ed-4840-a581-83e40c1e7630", "type": "concept", "title": "Social referencing"}], "description": "Infancy is a period of rapid change in perception, movement, communication, and social engagement."}, {"id": "808e29d9-8f4b-4534-88f9-fb24e5f95bb0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Attachment", "children": [{"id": "7d017d4e-9c72-4f4b-b351-13e36aaffbee", "type": "concept", "title": "Bowlby"}, {"id": "04282291-a71b-4afb-baea-5aeb603f43c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Ainsworth"}, {"id": "dd36e53a-8348-42d9-bc4c-58a2266df512", "type": "concept", "title": "Secure and insecure patterns"}, {"id": "96d2c6cc-d67e-447c-be5b-e09bf49e0118", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal working models"}], "description": "Attachment theory explains how early caregiver relationships support exploration, security, and regulation."}, {"id": "4f726a06-22c9-4777-af3b-b2b8632094e6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Temperament and Regulation", "children": [{"id": "425ae948-80c5-4621-90b1-67b05686bc15", "type": "concept", "title": "Reactivity"}, {"id": "0e3fb564-1976-43b5-ae53-338a0ace1388", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-soothing"}, {"id": "c50ab9b5-7ca8-4797-b51e-6e39f9080819", "type": "concept", "title": "Effortful control"}, {"id": "ca0ea776-eca6-4e56-9310-5175886d4ed2", "type": "concept", "title": "Caregiver responsiveness"}], "description": "Temperament helps explain early individual differences and the importance of goodness of fit."}]}, {"id": "39dc177d-eb43-4411-bd73-89693816ce2a", "type": "topic", "title": "Physical, Motor, Sensory, and Health Development", "description": "Connect growth, movement, sensory development, sleep, nutrition, and health to learning readiness and wellbeing.", "children": [{"id": "8d1653f3-35b1-47e8-bafa-a364aadf5b6b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Growth and Motor Development", "children": [{"id": "d0766c75-ad5c-4c5c-b6f1-7518313d66f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Gross motor skills"}, {"id": "6380cc49-71d6-495b-9551-efab0